# Trading Strategy Consistency
Rule Type: Prompt
Prompts: trading strategy, groq_recommendations, entry/exit logic, signal generation

## Core Principles
- Maintain identical entry/exit logic across all modes
- Ensure consistent signal generation
- Use shared methods for all trading operations
- Validate behavior across all modes

## Mode Consistency Rules
### Shared Requirements
- All modes must use identical:
  - Entry/exit logic
  - Signal generation parameters
  - Risk management rules
  - Indicator calculations
  - Zone identification logic

### Mode-Specific Requirements
#### Backtest Mode
- Must validate against historical data
- Must log all signals for comparison
- Must use same indicators as watch/realtime
- Must be reproducible

#### Watch Mode
- Must use identical signal generation as backtest
- Must log all signals for validation
- Must compare signals with backtest results
- Must validate against real-time data

#### Realtime Mode
- Must use identical signal generation as backtest/watch
- Must implement proper error handling
- Must log all operations for audit
- Must validate against market data

## Shared Methods
The following methods must be identical across all modes:
- `calculate_indicators`
- `identify_zones`
- `generate_signals`
- `generate_realtime_signals`
- `generate_exit_signals`

## Validation Requirements
### Signal Validation
- Backtest results must be reproducible in watch mode
- Watch mode signals must match backtest signals
- Realtime signals must follow same logic
- All signals must be logged for comparison

### Risk Management
- Stop loss rules must be identical
- Target profit rules must be identical
- Position sizing must be consistent
- Risk per trade must be identical

### Performance Validation
- Compare signal timing across modes
- Validate execution latency
- Monitor error rates
- Track performance metrics

## Implementation Guidelines
- No mode-specific entry/exit logic
- Use shared parameters for all modes
- Implement changes across all modes simultaneously
- Validate changes in all modes before deployment

## Documentation Requirements
- Document all shared methods
- Maintain change log
- Document validation results
- Track performance metrics

## Monitoring Requirements
- Monitor signal consistency
- Track execution latency
- Log all operations
- Maintain audit trail
